   "act": "cold open — Liam frames the Fourier square wave",
   "narration_text": "Any periodic function is a sum of sinusoids. A square wave decomposes into odd harmonics with decreasing amplitude — and as you add terms the sum converges, but it never kills the overshoot at the jump. That overshoot is the Gibbs phenomenon, and it never goes away.",
